ource":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/projection-specification/v1/definition.json","sha256":"42cff2435ac4e732bf0ea45a2e0f5d6fcdf2921f17b18bbd1b1adcc4e643eb24","version_ref":"cal.definition.projection-specification@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"PS-012","end_character":290,"excerpt":"View-bearing concept is not a vault node type, not an ontology branch by\nitself, not a lifecycle state, not a promotion state, and not a reason to create\na new tree for every term. It names the threshold where a concept needs a\ngoverned view because ordinary prose is no longer safe enough.","excerpt_sha256":"9bae4d24dc120bd3f500b21f6984be87f1339493d612793e5772c44f1af7a424","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Concept-not-ActualOwnerFidelity","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/boundary_conditions/0","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/projection-specification/v1/definition.json","sha256":"42cff2435ac4e732bf0ea45a2e0f5d6fcdf2921f17b18bbd1b1adcc4e643eb24","version_ref":"cal.definition.projection-specification@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"PS-013","end_character":419,"excerpt":"For concept `c`, `view_bearing(c)` is admissible when:\n\n```text\nview_bearing(c) =\n  distinct_evidence(c)\n  and lifecycle_posture_needed(c)\n  and owner_route(c)\n  and reuse_surface(c)\n  and challenge_or_drift_route(c)\n```\n\nThe view attached to `c` must declare allowed readings and forbidden authority\nmoves. If those fields are absent, `c` remains a term, candidate, or local\nconcept rather than a view-bearing concept.","excerpt_sha256":"c730e301f8b6ec58ac0df72a61e88133eef83b1fe35ccbd95c3b91f57f61efdd","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Concept-not-ActualViewHelpfulness","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/formal_expression","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/projection-specification/v1/definition.json","sha256":"42cff2435ac4e732bf0ea45a2e0f5d6fcdf2921f17b18bbd1b1adcc4e643eb24","version_ref":"cal.definition.projection-specification@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"PS-013","end_character":419,"excerpt":"For concept `c`, `view_bearing(c)` is admissible when:\n\n```text\nview_bearing(c) =\n  distinct_evidence(c)\n  and lifecycle_posture_needed(c)\n  and owner_route(c)\n  and reuse_surface(c)\n  and challenge_or_drift_route(c)\n```\n\nThe view attached to `c` must declare allowed readings and forbidden authority\nmoves. If those fields are absent, `c` remains a term, candidate, or local\nconcept rather than a view-bearing concept.","excerpt_sha256":"c730e301f8b6ec58ac0df72a61e88133eef83b1fe35ccbd95c3b91f57f61efdd","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Concept-not-ActualAuthority","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/formal_expression","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/projection-specification/v1/definition.json","sha256":"42cff2435ac4e732bf0ea45a2e0f5d6fcdf2921f17b18bbd1b1adcc4e643eb24","version_ref":"cal.definition.projection-specification@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"PS-013","end_character":419,"excerpt":"For concept `c`, `view_bearing(c)` is admissible when:\n\n```text\nview_bearing(c) =\n  distinct_evidence(c)\n  and lifecycle_posture_needed(c)\n  and owner_route(c)\n  and reuse_surface(c)\n  and challenge_or_drift_route(c)\n```\n\nThe view attached to `c` must declare allowed readings and forbidden authority\nmoves. If those fields are absent, `c` remains a term, candidate, or local\nconcept rather than a view-bearing concept.","excerpt_sha256":"c730e301f8b6ec58ac0df72a61e88133eef83b1fe35ccbd95c3b91f57f61efdd","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Concept-not-ActualFieldInterpretationFidelity","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/formal_expression","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/projection-specification/v1/definition.json","sha256":"42cff2435ac4e732bf0ea45a2e0f5d6fcdf2921f17b18bbd1b1adcc4e643eb24","version_ref":"cal.definition.projection-specification@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"PS-014","end_character":843,"excerpt":"Projection Specification is the normalized definition identified by semantic.projection-specification, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.definition. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D44 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nA view-bearing concept is a load-bearing concept that needs its own governed\nview or tree because it has distinct evidence, lifecycle posture, owner route,\nreuse surface, and challenge/drift behavior that cannot be safely handled as\nordinary narrative vocabulary.\n\nNot every term deserves a view. A concept may become view-bearing only when the\nview helps preserve evidence, relations, lifecycle, owner route, reuse, or\nchallenge behavior without pretending to decide authority by itself.","excerpt_sha256":"69c69565f543928b50da985583304c18bae2e34781d70c822e33ab461820454d","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Concept-not-ActualViewHelpfulness","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/normative_statement","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/projection-specification/v1/definition.json","sha256":"42cff2435ac4e732bf0ea45a2e0f5d6fcdf2921f17b18bbd1b1adcc4e643eb24","version_ref":"cal.definition.projection-specification@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"PS-014","end_character":843,"excerpt":"Projection Specification is the normalized definition identified by semantic.projection-specification, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.definition. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D44 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nA view-bearing concept is a load-bearing concept that needs its own governed\nview or tree because it has distinct evidence, lifecycle posture, owner route,\nreuse surface, and challenge/drift behavior that cannot be safely handled as\nordinary narrative vocabulary.\n\nNot every term deserves a view. A concept may become view-bearing only when the\nview helps preserve evidence, relations, lifecycle, owner route, reuse, or\nchallenge behavior without pretending to decide authority by itself.","excerpt_sha256":"69c69565f543928b50da985583304c18bae2e34781d70c822e33ab461820454d","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Concept-not-ActualAuthority","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/normative_statement","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.projection-specification","path":"evi